# Proxy the backend's sitemap/feed XML through this same domain — Google
# Search Console's "submit a sitemap" tool only accepts a path relative to
# the verified property, not an absolute URL on a different host, so a
# cross-domain sitemap URL submitted directly there gets silently truncated
# to a path and 404s against this frontend instead of reaching the backend.
# These four exact paths are proxied (not redirected — the URL in the
# browser/Search Console stays on this domain) straight through to the real
# backend routes; everything else is unaffected. See backend/src/routes/
# sitemap.routes.js and feed.routes.js for what actually generates these.
/api/sitemap-index.xml     https://noyon-telecom-api.onrender.com/api/sitemap-index.xml     200
/api/sitemap-pages.xml     https://noyon-telecom-api.onrender.com/api/sitemap-pages.xml     200
/api/sitemap-products.xml  https://noyon-telecom-api.onrender.com/api/sitemap-products.xml  200
/api/google-merchant.xml   https://noyon-telecom-api.onrender.com/api/google-merchant.xml   200

/*    /index.html   200
